extraction_notes: |
  - Transcribed from printed 71-73 (cache p072-p074) with the bonus lines, the
    P.P.E. line and the XP ladder read off renders. The ladder is the Battle
    Magus''s own column on printed 160; xp_table holds each band''s lower bound.
  - The book states two different spell rules. Ability 3 (printed 72) lists
    twenty initial spells and three offensive plus one defensive/evasion spell
    per level from level two, drawn from spell levels 1-4 until fifth level and
    from levels up to his own after. Ability 6 (printed 73) says he starts with
    10 spells of any level, can only cast spells at or below his experience
    level "like the Warlock", and is taught 2 spells per new level. The detailed
    ability 3 is stored; ability 6 is recorded here and not enforced. A few
    extra spells learned outside his career are seldom more than 1D4+4.
    Spell strength: standard.
  - Every granted spell resolves to an existing catalog row, cited to Rifts
    Book of Magic or Rifts Ultimate Edition (the survey''s Spells section).
  - "+2 to pull punch at levels 2, 4, 6, 9 and 13" is read as +2 gained at each
    listed level, the same way the book''s "+1 at levels ..." lines read. The
    render prints +2.
  - "+1 to save vs possession at levels 1, 3, 5 ... 15" and "+1 to save vs
    Horror Factor at levels 1, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8, 10, 12 and 14" are the level-one
    values in bonuses.saves and the rest in at_level. Save vs mind control is a
    flat +1.
  - Quick-draw initiative depends on P.P. and on the two chosen weapon types, so
    it is prose. So is +1 to aimed and called shots, and the half effect of
    confusion and dizziness.
  - The body armor (Standard Battler armor, 45 M.D.C., with a Demon helmet of 45
    M.D.C.) and the weapons (three ancient of choice, one ancient-style magic or
    TW weapon, two modern) have no catalog rows and stay in the Equipment
    section. Three weeks of rations are one food-rations entry; 50 feet of cord
    or rope is one lightweight-rope entry.
  - men_of_arms is false: the book files the class under its "Magus O.C.C.s"
    heading (printed 70), a school of magic.
---

## Lore

The Battle Magus, also known as the Battle Mage, is the front-line combat spell caster of Dweomer City''s troops, trained by the Brotherhood of Battle. A warrior first and a wizard second, he learns mastery of body, then of mind, then of magic, and his spells are almost entirely offensive. The Battle Magi are taught to respect and value life, so they are usually just, merciful and noble, and they respond to violence rather than instigate it. The lowest ranked of the four Magi and the most numerous, they are among the most feared warriors in the Magic Zone.

Battle Magi are often sent on scouting, exploration, spying and hunting missions, sometimes allowed to join outside groups of heroes, or to leave Dweomer as Sojourners. Leaving the service of Dweomer altogether is rare.

## Equipment

Clothes, uniform, ceremonial robes, utility belt, two canteens, backpack, knapsack, three weeks of food rations, a pair of handcuffs, 50 feet (15.2 m) of strong cord or rope, 1D4 flares, a flashlight, compass and pocket knife.

Standard Battler Body Armor (45 M.D.C.) and a Demon helmet (45 M.D.C., a pair of tiny horns and insect-looking eyes), of M.D.C. composite materials or magically created materials; not a full environmental suit.

Weapons: three ancient of choice (no special powers), one ancient-style magic or Techno-Wizard weapon, and two modern weapons. A Techno-Wizard weapon or other magic item may be awarded for heroics and on reaching levels 6, 10 and 15 in the Brotherhood''s service.

Money: as a member of the Dweomer Defense Force he has a furnished two-bedroom apartment, meals, uniforms, healing and access to the academies, plus 500 Universal Credits a month. Starts with 3D4x100 credits.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'battle-magus');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'battle-magus';

